    (0, None, '\'Viktor, good evening. Where is Alisa?\' "Kind evening" is the Russian, the sibling of "kind day". And "where Alisa" has no "is", as usual. Tanya is polite, and she is already suspicious.'),
    (1, None, '\'And she and I decided to stay.\' Russian says "we with her" for "she and I". It\'s a pattern you\'ve heard already. Barinov invents a plan on the spot, and he sounds very sure, which is how you can tell.'),
